WEBVTT

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:14.900
How can it be this late already?!

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:20.900
This is so bad!

00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:23.360
Have a good day!

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:26.470
Sorry to do this every morning, 
but I feel I need to repeat myself!

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:27.740
Wake me up, Mom!

00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:32.480
But Saki, you said "30 more 
minutes" three times...

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:34.600
30 more minutes, 30 more 
minutes, 30 more minutes...

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:38.530
Don't indulge your daughter's 
morning whining!

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:40.530
Okay!

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:43.180
You've been staying out so
 late every day, though...

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:44.470
Are you holding up all right?

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:49.350
Yeah... Now's the time I gotta 
buckle down and get through!

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:51.270
That's my Saki!

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:52.910
Well, see you later!

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:54.300
Ah, wait!

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:57.030
Take this if you need a pick-me-up.

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:58.100
Thanks.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:00:59.220
Well, see you later!

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:00.420
Have a good day!

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:05.840
Gotta hurry!

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:18.800
It seems the time may have come.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:22.760
Hey! Hey! Hey! Hey!

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:25.520
Open up, open up!

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:26.570
Excuse me—

00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:28.440
The hell happened?!

00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:31.430
No, don't tell me...

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:33.800
Please don't tell anyone about this.

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:36.440
I don't want her to know.

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:39.240
Sayo-chin...

00:01:48.070 --> 00:01:50.830
Mom's shabu-shabu is the best!

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:25.970
<b>Magical Girl - Lesson</b>

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:30.350
That's a wrap!

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:33.480
Magical Girl Ore-sama
Magical Girl Sakigasuki-sama
Green Room

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:33.480
Office

00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:43.340
<i>Saki, who had become an overnight 
sensation as an idol in her male form,</i>

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:45.480
<i>was filled with a burning regret.</i>

00:03:45.970 --> 00:03:48.990
Saki. The paparazzis got us again.

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:49.500
<b>Another bloodbath!</b>

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:49.500
<b>Unbeatable!
The magical girls are still here!</b>

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:49.500
<b>Countless enemies 
target magical girls</b>

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:53.620
Why did I have to run my big mouth?

00:03:55.850 --> 00:03:59.980
Our schedule used to be so
empty, and now it's packed.

00:04:00.710 --> 00:04:04.300
But to be honest, I have 
really mixed feelings...

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:08.510
And it feels like the more work
 we get, the more demons appear...

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:17.600
My Mohiro-chan...

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:21.140
Those demons flock to him like tissue 
pack soliciters around a station.

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:25.840
That life-work balance... is this 
what it means to be an idol?

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:27.620
Star Idol

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:39.040
<b>Countless enemies 
target magical girls</b>

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:39.040
<b>Another bloodbath!</b>

00:04:28.190 --> 00:04:30.260
Well, I guess it's like...

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:37.380
Any time we fight, it ends up in the paper, 
which results in us getting more work.

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:39.040
Ironically.

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:43.840
They've also caught me stepping 
in dog poo about ten times.

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:46.220
Who's happy to see that?

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:47.440
Who's the target audience?

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:49.120
Now, now.

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:51.930
Being busy just means you're popular!

00:04:52.260 --> 00:04:53.420
Manager...

00:04:53.420 --> 00:04:56.270
Look! Lots of new jobs in today!

00:04:56.270 --> 00:05:00.570
<b>Proposal</b>

00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:58.680
A questionable late-night drama,

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:03.140
a variety show, and a part in an
anime movie for you to read!

00:05:03.140 --> 00:05:04.570
Oh, by the way...

00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:07.770
Looks like we're getting these, too!

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:10.660
I just bought this in Ikebukuro!

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:14.160
Can I have this later?

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:16.160
No, never mind...

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:19.870
But of course, this is what 
idols are really about!

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:21.670
<b>Magical Girl 
Major Label Debut</b>

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:21.670
Recording Sample

00:05:19.870 --> 00:05:21.660
We're getting a major label debut!

00:05:22.310 --> 00:05:23.570
Really?

00:05:23.570 --> 00:05:26.430
At last, the major label I've been dreaming of!

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:28.090
I know, right?

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:31.820
At last, freed from the curse 
of having to buy my own stuff!

00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:35.370
We've always had to store all 
our CD backstock ourselves!

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:38.460
Sorry I had to lock you in to 
that purchasing contract!

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:42.100
Those CD boxes were taking up 
so much space in my house!

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:43.790
My room can't hold anymore!

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:44.840
Same here!

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:48.880
We're really getting our major label debut, then?

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:54.760
If this goes well, we might get an album, 
and maybe a magical girl documentary film...

00:05:55.930 --> 00:05:57.960
Things seem to be moving very quickly.

00:05:57.960 --> 00:06:05.340
<b>Magical Girl Major CD Debut</b>

00:05:58.260 --> 00:06:00.480
The CD industry is very competitive,

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:05.340
so projects line up quickly for anyone 
who's even slightly popular at the time.

00:06:05.750 --> 00:06:08.100
The value of the music is secondary, then?

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:09.350
Well, sorta.

00:06:09.350 --> 00:06:11.560
I hope I can sing it properly!

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:14.290
We haven't had proper singing 
practice in a while.

00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:16.810
Just approach it the way you normally do.

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:21.240
Besides, Saki-chan's never 
been a great singer.

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:23.110
Sakuyo-chan's fine...

00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:26.930
It seems a bit late in the game to be 
giving harsh feedback like that...

00:06:27.230 --> 00:06:31.540
It's probably a bit late to say this, too, 
but your dancing is also pretty freaky.

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:32.950
No wonder it didn't sell.

00:06:32.530 --> 00:06:33.960
Stop it!

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:36.750
I'm even starting to regret being born!

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:43.860
But you two really did shine when 
you were giving it your all.

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:46.160
That's what I've seen all this time.

00:06:57.820 --> 00:07:01.220
<i>I came to the city in search of 
the magical girls I loved so,</i>

00:07:01.830 --> 00:07:04.970
<i>but to my sorrow, I found none.</i>

00:07:11.770 --> 00:07:13.960
Why did I even come here?

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:15.990
I didn't know it would be like this...

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:20.910
<b>Featured Job Listings</b>

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:20.910
<b>Lalayu Pro, Inc</b>

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:20.910
<b>Editor's Pick</b>

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:20.910
Manager (Management Division)

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:20.920
Manager for idols, huh?

00:07:21.990 --> 00:07:25.240
<i>By chance, I found a listing 
for an idol manager.</i>

00:07:25.790 --> 00:07:29.970
<i>I got the job, and soon 
after, I met you two.</i>

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:39.890
Lalayu Pro, Inc
Management Division
Idol Manager
<b>Yamo Konami</b>

00:07:46.750 --> 00:07:51.510
We won't stop, we won't fail in pursuit 
of our dream! No one will beat us!

00:07:53.210 --> 00:07:56.160
<i>I took the manager job on a whim,</i>

00:07:56.160 --> 00:08:02.130
<i>but at some point, your enthusiasm 
had made me a real fan of yours.</i>

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:07.550
<i>They're so cool!</i>

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:09.730
<b>Aim For #1</b>

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:12.450
<b>Magical Twins</b>

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:13.490
<b>Honeyed Flash</b>

00:08:09.330 --> 00:08:13.970
<i>To be frank, there was even a moment when 
I thought the dream might be over...</i>

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:20.430
Final Notice

00:08:14.600 --> 00:08:16.530
Here it is, at last...

00:08:16.530 --> 00:08:20.430
But next week, they have that TV audition...

00:08:21.630 --> 00:08:24.510
<i>But you've been in the spotlight ever since!</i>

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:30.740
I'm so glad I stuck with you!

00:08:31.560 --> 00:08:35.080
I've been your biggest fan 
for the longest time.

00:08:35.800 --> 00:08:37.100
Manager...

00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:39.070
So...

00:08:39.730 --> 00:08:41.100
Let's get training!

00:08:41.100 --> 00:08:44.020
We've got no appointments today, 
so let's karaoke it up!

00:08:45.770 --> 00:08:46.780
'kay.

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:53.090
<b>Karaoke King</b>

00:08:53.250 --> 00:08:55.240
10,000 feet up in the Alps,

00:08:55.240 --> 00:08:57.220
standing on Koyari Peak,

00:08:57.220 --> 00:08:59.120
let us dance an Alpine dance,

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:00.780
let us dance together!

00:09:00.780 --> 00:09:01.200
Hey!

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:10.720
Last night I had some dreams,

00:09:10.720 --> 00:09:12.600
little dreams and big ones!

00:09:12.600 --> 00:09:14.600
I put them away in my pack,

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:16.240
and climbed up to Mt. Fuji!

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:24.540
Hey!

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:29.690
H-How was it?

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:35.740
About like an amateur 
playing karaoke master.

00:09:35.740 --> 00:09:37.310
Minus 52 points.

00:09:37.980 --> 00:09:39.210
He's harsh.

00:09:40.420 --> 00:09:44.540
I keep seeing signs of self-consciousness.

00:09:44.540 --> 00:09:46.490
You need to knock off the innocent act.

00:09:46.490 --> 00:09:49.680
<i>My manager told me I'm putting 
up an innocent act...</i>

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:50.940
<b>Urgent Announcement</b>

00:09:51.430 --> 00:09:54.660
<i>This is our new song, Love Shock!</i>

00:09:54.660 --> 00:09:56.320
<i>Now on sale!</i>

00:09:57.480 --> 00:09:58.700
It's PRISMA!

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:00.440
I gotta buy their new single!

00:10:00.440 --> 00:10:02.860
Manager, you've got such varied tastes...

00:10:02.860 --> 00:10:05.440
Well, I need to follow what 
other agencies are up to.

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:08.420
That's top idols for you! They're so good...

00:10:08.420 --> 00:10:09.790
What are you talking about?

00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:13.450
You're going to overtake them soon enough!

00:10:13.770 --> 00:10:14.780
Now, next up.

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:16.710
Sakuyo-chan. How about a solo?

00:10:17.060 --> 00:10:18.940
Well, then...

00:10:18.940 --> 00:10:22.210
I love Saki... Saki... Saki.

00:10:26.720 --> 00:10:27.440
Huh?

00:10:27.440 --> 00:10:28.290
What?

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:34.210
Please listen to this song
I stayed up all last night to write.

00:10:34.210 --> 00:10:35.360
"I Love Saki."

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:37.370
Yeah, it figures!

00:10:42.360 --> 00:10:46.080
Saki Saki Saki... Saki...

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:48.510
Saki, Sa-kiss me...

00:10:48.090 --> 00:10:50.490
<i>These lyrics she wrote... somehow,</i>

00:10:50.490 --> 00:10:53.540
<i>you can just tell that she and 
Mohiro-chan are related...</i>

00:10:54.030 --> 00:10:57.640
<i>And why did she bother transforming?</i>

00:10:57.640 --> 00:11:02.360
Saki, if you mistake me for my brother 
and we make a mistake together...

00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:03.840
I'm okay with that.

00:11:02.380 --> 00:11:04.920
Manager, please offer your opinion!

00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:06.170
Let's see...

00:11:06.170 --> 00:11:10.790
It's good for you to write original songs, 
and I like the emotion you put into it,

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:14.100
but you failed to engage with the audience,

00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:15.940
so I have to give you a minus three or so.

00:11:16.410 --> 00:11:18.710
Just minus three?

00:11:18.710 --> 00:11:20.690
How bad am I, then?

00:11:21.440 --> 00:11:22.750
Well, all right, then.

00:11:22.750 --> 00:11:24.570
I'll have to show you a sample.

00:11:24.570 --> 00:11:26.690
Let me borrow that CD player.

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:28.490
Oh, certainly.

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:29.600
<b>Magical Twins</b>

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:29.960
<b>Honeyed Flash</b>

00:11:34.330 --> 00:11:38.070
<i>That's right. I've never seen 
our manager sing before...</i>

00:11:38.070 --> 00:11:41.120
<i>After all that talk, he'd 
better be pretty good.</i>

00:11:41.660 --> 00:11:45.330
<i>If he's awful, maybe I'll 
take him to task a little!</i>

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:55.060
Everyone! I'm Pinky Konamin!

00:11:55.540 --> 00:11:58.310
Let's raise the roof!

00:11:58.990 --> 00:12:02.660
What's with this adorable MCing?

00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:05.070
<i>He even seems to have a
totally different bone structure!</i>

00:12:07.720 --> 00:12:12.340
<i>I wanna be the kind of 
girl who's in style...</i>

00:12:13.570 --> 00:12:18.130
<i>So why is it that I always get hurt?</i>

00:12:13.760 --> 00:12:16.770
Woah... he's even better than I thought.

00:12:18.520 --> 00:12:22.040
<i>My fortunes always say "worst luck!"</i>

00:12:22.040 --> 00:12:24.580
<i>When I try to act stylish, I fall on my butt!</i>

00:12:23.250 --> 00:12:25.250
And... are there three of him there?

00:12:24.580 --> 00:12:29.090
<i>That's my life: all bad luck and sadness!</i>

00:12:25.250 --> 00:12:26.090
Oh...

00:12:26.090 --> 00:12:28.010
No, Saki, that's...

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:28.890
Can it be...

00:12:29.090 --> 00:12:35.140
<i>When I eat bread with honey, 
I always drop it...</i>

00:12:29.610 --> 00:12:34.240
He's moving at super speed to play three 
different roles with his afterimages!

00:12:34.910 --> 00:12:38.430
Hey! It makes me sad when 
you're not looking at me!

00:12:35.140 --> 00:12:38.440
<i>And why does it always fall honey side down?</i>

00:12:38.750 --> 00:12:40.950
He knows how to hold on 
to the audience, too!

00:12:40.950 --> 00:12:43.590
<i>Go for it! Oh, me!</i>

00:12:41.940 --> 00:12:45.850
<i>Amazing... I'm sorry for saying 
those things about you.</i>

00:12:42.150 --> 00:12:47.450
<b>The working idol feels inadequate</b>

00:12:43.590 --> 00:12:46.700
<i>If only I had a magic spell...</i>

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:49.190
<i>I like you! Oh, you!</i>

00:12:49.190 --> 00:12:50.190
Oh, hello!

00:12:49.190 --> 00:12:52.500
<i>My love could change me!</i>

00:12:50.190 --> 00:12:52.120
I ordered orange juice...

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:52.940
Huh?

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:55.090
<i>I believe I can do anything if I try!</i>

00:12:52.940 --> 00:12:54.670
I ordered oolong tea.

00:12:55.090 --> 00:12:57.250
Tropical fruit here!

00:12:58.160 --> 00:13:01.080
<i>I love you! Oh, you!</i>

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:04.230
<i>I can do anything!</i>

00:13:04.230 --> 00:13:07.600
<i>Let's go, let's go! Just watch!</i>

00:13:04.330 --> 00:13:07.600
Why didn't anyone comment on that?!

00:13:07.600 --> 00:13:09.230
<i>That's my "Honeyed Flash!"</i>

00:13:08.380 --> 00:13:09.240
On what?

00:13:09.240 --> 00:13:14.230
The guy who brought in our drinks was the 
weirdo with the supermarket bag over his face!

00:13:14.230 --> 00:13:15.610
Sorry, I didn't notice.

00:13:15.610 --> 00:13:16.820
How could you not notice?!

00:13:16.820 --> 00:13:18.450
Am I the crazy one here?!

00:13:18.450 --> 00:13:20.240
Oh? What's the matter?

00:13:20.240 --> 00:13:22.440
Seriously, what is with that guy?!

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:23.570
Probably working part-time?

00:13:23.570 --> 00:13:25.120
He did say he was poor.

00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:26.430
We're done here!

00:13:39.340 --> 00:13:41.350
Ko-san, stop it...

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:46.300
Sayo-chin, your body's telling 
a different story...

00:13:55.460 --> 00:13:57.200
Oh, yes! Right there!

00:13:57.570 --> 00:14:00.030
Here? Is that where you want it?

00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:04.770
No! Oh, oh!

00:14:04.770 --> 00:14:07.440
Your mouth says no, but your body...

00:14:09.150 --> 00:14:11.040
Ko-san, I'm...

00:14:11.040 --> 00:14:11.810
Sayo-chin!

00:14:29.460 --> 00:14:31.760
You could see that coming, couldn't you?

00:14:31.760 --> 00:14:34.840
It's such a cliché. Is there 
really demand for this crap?

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:38.480
<b>Contract</b>

00:14:38.710 --> 00:14:41.410
Just shut up and put your stamp on it.

00:14:42.940 --> 00:14:45.310
Your daughter's maturing quickly.

00:14:45.310 --> 00:14:48.190
She's a suitable successor to you.

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:52.490
Your body's a wreck, 
and your back especially.

00:14:52.930 --> 00:14:54.930
You don't need to keep forcing yourself.

00:14:55.690 --> 00:14:57.810
You think it's time?

00:14:58.530 --> 00:15:01.620
You've done more than 
your share for the area.

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:04.940
Leave things to your daughter from now on.

00:15:05.570 --> 00:15:08.370
So I've become a bother to you, have I?

00:15:09.060 --> 00:15:10.230
No way!

00:15:11.090 --> 00:15:12.540
Just kidding!

00:15:12.540 --> 00:15:15.770
Thank you, Ko-san, for 
always worrying about me.

00:15:17.280 --> 00:15:18.640
A little token of my appreciation.

00:15:18.640 --> 00:15:20.300
Just shut up and accept it, okay?

00:15:20.740 --> 00:15:23.190
We can cancel the contract 
today, if you want.

00:15:23.190 --> 00:15:26.050
You can go back to a civilian life.

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:27.310
What's your call?

00:15:29.980 --> 00:15:31.310
One week longer.

00:15:33.290 --> 00:15:34.370
Ko-san.

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:38.970
Let me enjoy one last 
week as a magical girl.

00:15:41.240 --> 00:15:43.690
Well, think about it.

00:15:43.690 --> 00:15:46.900
I'd better go home and get some shut-eye.

00:15:59.430 --> 00:16:01.540
Am I really getting my major label debut?

00:16:01.540 --> 00:16:03.470
I wonder how the recording will go...

00:16:03.940 --> 00:16:06.160
Will the director be scary?

00:16:06.160 --> 00:16:08.970
Oh, I'm getting so nervous!

00:16:17.260 --> 00:16:18.990
Oh? That was fast.

00:16:18.990 --> 00:16:20.860
Yeah, it's fine...

00:16:21.320 --> 00:16:22.990
Let's get back to the room.

00:16:27.050 --> 00:16:28.410
I'm ba—

00:16:28.410 --> 00:16:30.390
<i>10,000 feet up in the Alps,</i>

00:16:30.390 --> 00:16:32.080
<i>standing on Koyari Peak,</i>

00:16:32.080 --> 00:16:34.050
<i>let us dance an Alpine dance,</i>

00:16:34.050 --> 00:16:35.750
<i>let us dance together!</i>

00:16:35.750 --> 00:16:38.180
Mudskipper... I mean, Mohiro-chan!

00:16:38.430 --> 00:16:39.750
What is he doing here?

00:16:39.750 --> 00:16:43.430
Did he learn how to teleport 
without telling me?!

00:16:43.740 --> 00:16:45.600
Saki, it's the wrong room.

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:46.550
It's next door.

00:16:46.810 --> 00:16:48.200
O-Of course it is...

00:16:48.610 --> 00:16:51.840
<i>But it's such a coincidence that our rooms 
would be next door to each other...</i>

00:16:51.840 --> 00:16:55.850
<i>Could this be... destiny?!</i>

00:16:57.530 --> 00:17:01.250
<i>I want to listen to Mohiro-chan's 
children's song medley forever!</i>

00:17:01.250 --> 00:17:05.360
<i>I wanna stay here forever! I don't 
wanna go back to my room!</i>

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:07.930
Saki. You're being creepy.

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:13.230
That's it! I need a spell to 
swap bodies with Hyoe!

00:17:13.230 --> 00:17:15.250
Not happening. Leave now.

00:17:16.830 --> 00:17:18.220
Saki, your panties are on display.

00:17:55.470 --> 00:17:57.860
Wow, monster house.

00:17:57.860 --> 00:18:00.390
I love Mohiro-chan.

00:18:01.120 --> 00:18:03.760
Kokoro-chan-san, my weapon.

00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:09.020
Hey, don't call me while I'm in the bath!

00:18:09.020 --> 00:18:10.970
My weapon, if you please.

00:18:10.970 --> 00:18:12.020
R-Right.

00:18:21.630 --> 00:18:24.940
Okay, time to clean house.

00:18:24.940 --> 00:18:25.910
Yeah.

00:18:29.330 --> 00:18:31.650
One more round!

00:18:33.320 --> 00:18:36.890
Getting pretty sloppy in how you fight, eh?

00:18:37.410 --> 00:18:40.100
Hey! I'm telling the BPO on you!

00:18:57.510 --> 00:19:00.550
I had a feeling this would happen.

00:19:01.310 --> 00:19:05.820
You're really at home with this 
whole slaughter thing now, huh?

00:19:07.370 --> 00:19:09.900
It looks like a barbecue.

00:19:09.900 --> 00:19:12.220
What? Are demons edible?

00:19:20.420 --> 00:19:21.980
What was it, defective?

00:19:21.980 --> 00:19:23.200
As if!

00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:25.100
What have you done, idiot?!

00:19:25.620 --> 00:19:28.680
Huh? The stick just broke, didn't it?

00:19:28.680 --> 00:19:32.180
You were too hard on it!

00:19:32.180 --> 00:19:36.390
Damn... teenagers these days 
don't know when to stop.

00:19:36.390 --> 00:19:38.440
Sayo-chin would never fight like this.

00:19:43.510 --> 00:19:45.090
Nothing.

00:19:45.090 --> 00:19:47.960
You have plenty of 
replacement sticks, don't you?

00:19:48.700 --> 00:19:50.000
Don't be stupid.

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:53.460
It'll take a long time to find and order
 a new one from the warehouse.

00:19:53.460 --> 00:19:55.840
Oh, really?

00:19:55.840 --> 00:19:57.590
Sakuyo, can I borrow yours?

00:19:57.590 --> 00:19:59.880
I fight bare-handed. Melee only.

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:01.710
Oh, that's right...

00:20:02.020 --> 00:20:06.670
Besides, the magical power flowing 
through each weapon is different.

00:20:06.670 --> 00:20:11.720
It ain't easy to find a good weapon 
attuned to your particular magic.

00:20:12.160 --> 00:20:14.040
I didn't know that...

00:20:14.040 --> 00:20:18.530
I'd love it if my next stick 
was a more glittery one!

00:20:18.530 --> 00:20:21.980
And what'll happen if demons 
attack in the meantime?!

00:20:21.980 --> 00:20:23.920
Show a little concern, dumbass!

00:20:29.520 --> 00:20:32.020
Hey, I was just thinking...

00:20:34.110 --> 00:20:37.120
The demons appeared near 
my brother again today.

00:20:37.480 --> 00:20:38.950
Yeah...

00:20:38.950 --> 00:20:41.130
It must be pretty rough on Mohiro-chan, huh?

00:20:41.130 --> 00:20:44.150
And picked some flowers in the field!

00:20:44.530 --> 00:20:49.250
Do you think the boss of the monsters 
might be closer than we think?

00:20:50.260 --> 00:20:54.770
After all, they always seem to 
know just where my brother is.

00:20:55.300 --> 00:20:58.400
Their karaoke party today was 
probably private, right?

00:20:59.410 --> 00:21:00.340
Which means...

00:21:10.140 --> 00:21:12.020
Which means... what?

00:21:12.020 --> 00:21:13.760
You really are stupid, ain't ya?

00:21:14.150 --> 00:21:15.850
Here's the next round.

00:21:15.850 --> 00:21:17.180
Don't slack off.

00:21:24.000 --> 00:21:25.660
All that singing wiped me out!

00:21:25.660 --> 00:21:27.250
Hey, where are the girls?

00:21:27.880 --> 00:21:30.570
Wow, look at all those calls!

00:23:20.000 --> 00:23:35.010
<b>Preview</b>

00:23:20.760 --> 00:23:25.280
<i>At last, the magical girls have clawed 
their way up to the meet-and-greet!</i>

00:23:25.280 --> 00:23:29.020
<i>Demons, carve this love into your bodies!</i>

00:23:29.550 --> 00:23:32.090
<i>Next time, "Magical Girl - Meet-and-Greet."</i>

00:23:30.010 --> 00:23:35.010
<b>Magical Girl - Meet-and-Greet</b>

00:23:32.410 --> 00:23:34.660
<i>You are already shaking my hand.</i>

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.020
Illustration: Monokubo
